tinacloud-configure(1) -- Configure a local Tina project
========================================================

## DESCRIPTION

Most commands require you to pass in your TinaCloud organization ID and/or
project ID. To make this process less repetitive, if inside a TinaCMS project,
running `tinacloud configure` will write these two IDs to
`<project-root>/<tina-dir>/tinacloud.json`. 

Once written, commands that require any of these two values will attempt to
read from said file first.

## SYNOPSIS

`tinacloud configure`

## OPTIONS

  * `--org-id`:
    TinaCloud organization ID

  * `--project-id`:
    TinaCloud project ID

  * `--tina-dir`:
    Path to the tina folder (default "tina")

## EXAMPLES

Interactively choose a project for the TinaCMS project in the current directory:

	$ tinacloud configure

Configure the current project without a prompt:

	$ tinacloud configure \
		--org-id <organization-id> \
		--project-id <project-id>

Use a Tina directory other than the default:

	$ tinacloud configure \
		--org-id <organization-id> \
		--project-id <project-id> \
		--tina-dir .tina

